<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Local-dev entitlements for ad-hoc-signed builds produced by
    Scripts/build-app.sh without SIGNING_IDENTITY set. macOS 26
    (Tahoe) tightened sandbox-profile compilation: a sandboxed app
    whose entitlements include team-bound capabilities
    (com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers,
    com.apple.security.application-groups) but whose signature lacks
    a matching provisioning profile fails to launch with
    "Launchd job spawn failed" (NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=163).

    So local ad-hoc builds intentionally ship with NO entitlements
    (empty dict): the dev binary has the same filesystem access as
    any user-owned process, and iCloud Drive sync falls back to the
    local Application Support path (each dev build sees only its own
    camera list). Network client + microphone access just work —
    those capabilities don't need entitlements outside the sandbox.

    The shipping App Store build does NOT use this file. It uses
    App/Reolens.appstore.entitlements, which carries the full
    sandbox + iCloud + CloudKit + App Group entitlements; AMFI
    validates those against the App Store provisioning profile that
    xcodebuild embeds at archive time.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
